    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Dongpo pork demands a piece of pork belly with equal layers of fat and lean meat. The slow braise in wine renders the fat completely, while the collagen from the skin creates a thick, syrupy "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "braising-liquid"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "braising liquid "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blanching-pork"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "blanching"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " step at the start is not optional. It removes a strong porky smell that would otherwise dominate the finished dish. A traditional "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "clay-pot"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "clay pot"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " gives the best result, but a dutch oven works well."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
